[statement]
A name whose other candidates are ruled out requires what the one left
depends on with the constraints it states, as a name with a single
candidate from the start does
(`a-sole-candidate-s-dependency-is-required-with-its-constraint`): `pc:g`
has two candidates, which share `g`, and `sv`, whose one candidate needs
`pc:g>=4`, rules out `gd` 3. `gd` 4 is then the only one, and its
`g=4` is required before `g` is decided; apk installs `g` 4, though `g` 5
is offered.

[repository]
P:g
V:4

P:g
V:5

P:gd
V:3
D:g
p:pc:g=3

P:gd
V:4
D:g=4
p:pc:g=4

P:sv
V:7
D:pc:g>=4
p:pc:sv=7

P:t
V:1
D:sv pc:g>=3 pc:sv>=6

[request]
t

[answer apk-tools 3.0.9-r0]
install g 4
install gd 4
install sv 7
install t 1
